which Netfabric Acquisition Corp. was merged with and into Old Xcel, with Old Xcel surviving as a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company. On September 29, 2011, we changed our name to Xcel Brands, Inc.","context":"Company History and Corporate Information","section":"Item 1. Business","block":76,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"526c3eb45b06e0dbe3ea0e5873e55d9080e9d03b102323b1660282cd146504cc","quote":"On March 24, 2025, the Company filed an amendment to its Amended and Restated Certificate of Incorporation to effect a one-for-ten (1:10) reverse stock split of the shares of the Company’s common stock. As a result of this reverse stock split, effective March 24, 2025, every ten (10) shares of our issued and outstanding common stock were automatically combined into one (1) issued and outstanding share of common stock, without any change in the par value per share or number of shares authorized. No fractional shares were issued, and the shares of common stock underlying the Company’s outstanding stock options and warrants were also proportionately adjusted along with corresponding adjustments to their exercise prices. The reverse stock split was primarily intended to bring the Company in compliance with the minimum bid requirement to maintain listing of its common stock on the NASDAQ Capital Market. We have reflected the reverse split on a retroactive basis to all applicable amounts contained in this Annual Report on Form 10-K.","context":"The Company was incorporated on August 31, 1989 in the State of Delaware under the name Houston Operating Company. On April 19, 2005, we changed our name to NetFabric Holdings, Inc. On September 29, 2011, Xcel Brands, Inc., a privately-held Delaware corporation (which we refer to as Old Xcel), Netfabric Acquisition Corp., a Delaware corporation and wholly owned subsidiary of the Company, and certain stockholders of the Company entered into an agreement of merger and plan of reorganization pursuant to which Netfabric Acquisition Corp. was merged with and into Old Xcel, with Old Xcel surviving as a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company. On September 29, 2011, we changed our name to Xcel Brands, Inc.","section":"Item 1. Business","block":77,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"bdd6407a19dcd36ee98cc658488b7035a791554e89d2b315c34fd91bc270e0cb","quote":"Our principal office is currently located at 550 Seventh Avenue, 11th Floor, New York, NY 10018.","context":"On March 24, 2025, the Company filed an amendment to its Amended and Restated Certificate of Incorporation to effect a one-for-ten (1:10) reverse stock split of the shares of the Company’s common stock. As a result of this reverse stock split, effective March 24, 2025, every ten (10) shares of our issued and outstanding common stock were automatically combined into one (1) issued and outstanding share of common stock, without any change in the par value per share or number of shares authorized. No fractional shares were issued, and the shares of common stock underlying the Company’s outstanding stock options and warrants were also proportionately adjusted along with corresponding adjustments to their exercise prices. The reverse stock split was primarily intended to bring the Company in compliance with the minimum bid requirement to maintain listing of its common stock on the NASDAQ Capital Market. We have reflected the reverse split on a retroactive basis to all applicable amounts contained in this Annual Report on Form 10-K.","section":"Item 1. Business","block":78,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"5796a8367f3afa98eeba7902133f80d894a4f489aca6ff773de754cfab092530","quote":"The Halston brand was founded by Roy Halston Frowick in the 1960s, and quickly became one of the most important American fashion brands in the world, becoming synonymous with glamour, sophistication, and femininity. Halston’s groundbreaking designs and visionary style still influence designers around the world today. We acquired the H Halston brands in December 2014, and since our acquisition of the Halston Heritage brands in February 2019, we own all Halston labels under our brands. The Halston brand is available across various distribution channels – including premium and","context":"Halston","section":"Item 1. Business","block":83,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-2025123