ilco Global is the sole Class A Member of LL, and Xcel is the sole Class B Member of LL (each individually a “Member”). Each Member holds a 50% equity ownership interest in LL; however, based on an analysis of the contractual terms and rights contained in the agreements between the Members, the Company has previously determined that under the applicable accounting standards, LL is a variable interest entity and the Company has effective control over LL. Therefore, as the primary beneficiary, the Company has consolidated LL since 2019, and has recognized the assets, liabilities, revenues, and expenses of LL as part of its consolidated financial statements, along with a noncontrolling interest which represents Hilco Global’s 50% ownership share in LL.","context":"Longaberger Licensing, LLC Variable Interest Entity","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":955,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"a2d35a1f0e20859f3fb01abe83bbf5c636a5fbbec2738c58e9d0ce88b49b924d","quote":"On June 21, 2024, the Company (through its wholly owned subsidiary, Gold Licensing, LLC) entered into an asset purchase agreement with Lori Goldstein and Lori Goldstein, Ltd (together the “LG Parties”), pursuant to which the Company agreed to sell, and the LG Parties agreed to purchase, substantially all of the assets of the Lori Goldstein Brand, including the “LOGO by Lori Goldstein” trademark and other intellectual property rights relating thereto. Also in conjunction with this transaction, key license agreements related to the Lori Goldstein Brand were assigned to and assumed by the LG Parties. This divestiture transaction closed on June 30, 2024.","context":"Divestiture of the Lori Goldstein Brand","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":957,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"dfddab14ed2f7c9c2e8fddc15ae0b123413d642a301d835b58b4c40a0ec35426","quote":"As consideration for the sale of these assets, the parties agreed to the following:","context":"On June 21, 2024, the Company (through its wholly owned subsidiary, Gold Licensing, LLC) entered into an asset purchase agreement with Lori Goldstein and Lori Goldstein, Ltd (together the “LG Parties”), pursuant to which the Company agreed to sell, and the LG Parties agreed to purchase, substantially all of the assets of the Lori Goldstein Brand, including the “LOGO by Lori Goldstein” trademark and other intellectual property rights relating thereto. Also in conjunction with this transaction, key license agreements related to the Lori Goldstein Brand were assigned to and assumed by the LG Parties. This divestiture transaction closed on June 30, 2024.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":958,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"f81fc2a2f117bd552034cc502ad2d329a73331f0920ff50f50d05e28ca3f87a9","quote":"●The LG Parties waived their rights with respect to certain contingent consideration amounts that had been previously earned by the LG Parties (under the terms of the April 1, 2021 purchase of the assets by Xcel), and terminated their rights to any future earn-out payments.","context":"As consideration for the sale of these assets, the parties agreed to the following:","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":959,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"d81657adc9674c7ab8a4f627014d3f662d35d5b0c983c8e01338a0b9b4a15d18","quote":"●The Company retained the right to all royalties and fee income for net sales from licensees related to the Lori Goldstein Brand through the closing date.","context":"●The LG Parties waived their rights with respect to certain contingent consideration amounts that had been previously earned by the LG Parties (under the terms of the April 1, 2021 purchase of the assets by Xcel), and terminated their rights to any future earn-out payments.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":960,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"bfdd45729c6f9eaeac639a203affbc3493698c0f70da137c9e5f6503e8888f51","quote":"●The Company’s May 2, 2024 termination of the employment agreement and consulting agreement with the LG Parties was withdrawn. The Company paid the LG Parties a combined total of $25,000 as compensation for services rendered under the employment agreement and consulting agreement through June 30, 2024, and also reimbursed Ms. Goldstein for expenses incurred in the course of fulfilling her duties under the employment agreement through June 30, 2024.","context":"●The Company retained the right to all royalties and fee income for net sales from licensees related to the Lori Goldstein Brand through the closing date.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":961,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"5d95b40a4828bfca1c2da6a2757e5a6312156f09cc2cfb06581a32ee669bb502","quote":"●The Company and the LG Parties entered into a mutual general release and waiver of outstanding legal disputes.","context":"●The Company’s May 2, 2024 termination of the employment agreement and consulting agreement with the LG Parties was withdrawn. The Company paid the LG Parties a combined total of $25,000 as compensation for services rendered under the employment agreement and consulting agreement through June 30, 2024, and also reimbursed Ms. Goldstein for expenses incurred in the course of fulfilling her duties under the employment agreement through June 30, 2024.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":962,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926043348/xelb-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09.bin","sha256":"0b0a8f8d4dbfba528598f52fcc783f8e4a9691939edc3ae4905c0bee51370a09"}},{"id":"f1d8361c22fcb59bd77b29167c8f875492d6e99a65b2b040b51c0018848e94bd","quote":"The total consideration received by the Company for this divestiture transaction was approximately $6.08 million, comprised of (i) the waiver of approximately $1.03 million of accrued earn-out payments earned by the LG Parties through June 30, 2024, plus (ii) the release of the remaining balance of approximately $5.05 million of contingent obligations recorded on the Company’s balance sheet. The remaining unamortized net book value of the Lori Goldstein intangible assets immediately prior to the sale was approximately $1.93 million, and the Company also incurred approximately $0.35 million of legal fees in connection with this transaction. Accordingly, the Company recorded a net non-cash gain on the divestiture of the Lori Goldstein Brand of approximately $3.80 million for the year ended December 31, 2024.","context":"●The Company and the LG Parties entered into a mutual general release and waiver of outstanding legal disputes.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":963,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-043348","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://w